From 86e4855590e136cf0195714a4db215e204ad1a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teemu Haila <teemu.haila@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:16:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/36] drm/amd/display: GPU-scaled lower resolutions on the
 stitched iMac 5K panel

The stitched root exposed only the 5120x2880 mode. Add the resolutions macOS
offers on this iMac (4096x2304 ... 1280x720) plus common 16:10 and 4:3 ones.
They keep the native stitched timing; the display scaler fits each onto the
panel (aspect-preserving, centred). Each tile stream composes one half of the
CRTC mode, (0,0,W/2,H), scaled onto its part of the fit rectangle
(amdgpu_dm_tiled_stitch_split_scaling()); the plane split and the peer cursor
shift now use that half-mode width instead of the tile timing width. For the
native mode the result is the previous 1:1 split. mode_valid rejects a
stitched-root mode whose stream is not on the tile timing.

[adapter: iMac20 PoC, REVIEW.md L6 (fallback modes), owner request]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 233 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 187 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

